[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88831"] :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the event that the chosen component was produced by machine $A$, and let $D$ be the event that the chosen component is defective. Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the component was produced by machine $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that the randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(D\\cap A),$ we take the number of defective components produced by machine $A,$ and divide by the total number of defective components $(37+43=80).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap A)=\\frac{5}{80}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(D\\cap {A}^{′}),$ we take the number of defective components produced by machine $B,$ and divide by the total number of defective components $(37+43=80).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(D\\cap {A}^{′})=\\frac{3}{80}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected component is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{80}+\\frac{3}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "b475f41a-bb0b-5847-8d34-af0fea8a3238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a" :answer/id #uuid "02fd9981-6671-5bd6-b00a-38c15401e241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "4906c734-dedd-5ab2-a21c-58d004ccc6bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "8828c272-930b-5713-84d7-7096938a8219" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "b34226e7-213c-503b-bd3d-25acd14c549d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "382551a3-dd9e-5b40-baff-e11b9ef7542f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88918/selection/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a" :answer-field/choices ["q-88918/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-88918/selection/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a" "q-88918/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-88918/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-88918/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88918" :question/id #uuid "9db4b0ac-3bb0-5844-ad10-5311f4573d6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-88918" :question/problem "A pet center registered $34$ dogs and $29$ cats on a particular day. Of the dogs registered that day, $12$ were vaccinated. Of the cats registered that day, $15$ were vaccinated. What is the probability that a randomly selected pet registered that day was vaccinated?" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the event that the chosen pet was vaccinated, and let $D$ be the event that the pet is a dog. Then ${D}^{′}$ is the event that the pet is a cat.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected pet was vaccinated, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(V)=P(V\\cap D)+P(V\\cap {D}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(V\\cap D),$ we take the number of dogs who visited the pet center and were vaccinated $(12)$ and divide by the total number of pets $(34+29=63).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(V\\cap D)=\\frac{12}{63}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(V\\cap {D}^{′}),$ we take the number of cats who visited the pet center and were vaccinated $(15)$ and divide by the total number of pets $(63).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(V\\cap {D}^{′})=\\frac{15}{63}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected pet was vaccinated is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V\\cap D)+P(V\\cap {D}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{63}+\\frac{15}{63} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{63} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88918/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "dc43f80b-b158-58c4-a2e9-559d5b0115ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "832589f0-03d9-588e-8a23-4a846274c098" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "1a16aa56-bbe5-5f20-867a-26d774905b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "939098bb-7fec-54d4-ac4f-99342bdd68f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "1052fac3-7be4-52fd-b8ec-a3c8a43fd226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "37c118bc-25fb-527f-8d09-2226a28ecd1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88916/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer-field/choices ["q-88916/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" "q-88916/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-88916/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-88916/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-88916/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88916" :question/id #uuid "122759e3-2f34-5855-9414-74d10d38758c" :question/math-academy-id "q-88916" :question/problem "William has a desk with two drawers, $A$ and $B.$ In drawer $A$ he has $14$ markers, of which $3$ are blue. In drawer $B$ he has $21$ markers, of which $4$ are blue. What is the probability that a randomly selected marker from either drawer is blue?" :question/worked-solution "Let $U$ be the event that the chosen marker is blue, and let $A$ be the event that the marker was selected from drawer $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the marker was selected from drawer $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected marker is blue, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(U)=P(U\\cap A)+P(U\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(U\\cap A),$ we take the number of blue markers in drawer $A$ $(3)$ and divide by the total number of markers in both drawers $(14+21=35).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(U\\cap A)=\\frac{3}{35}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(U\\cap {A}^{′}),$ we take the number of blue markers on drawer $B$ $(4)$ and divide by the total number of markers in both drawers $(35).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(U\\cap {A}^{′})=\\frac{4}{35}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected marker from the desk drawers is blue is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U) & =P(U\\cap A)+P(U\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{35}+\\frac{4}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88916/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection/5df1e722e09c055a88f8288a681d6644451c9bb1bc22bf81932e0643a8a535ff" :answer/id #uuid "547cc467-564b-5b2f-a9f5-c395df6c836e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{51}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection/937298cd9018b16cda053ff5c1f82aa544378413cbcd38ce309be5777298b48a" :answer/id #uuid "37db604f-5fd2-5139-8e8e-fe23cddac683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{102}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection/befe5c309efbebd1f8cf046225b6752c361c4232623e8d3c63a7f3230bd5fe6c" :answer/id #uuid "d2d290e9-2f77-525a-bf97-0827cbe5e6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{51}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "834602d8-dd0b-561e-be86-aa5dc467b012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection/36c923422d0040a751574fbe850eee2f3de5e3ee5e9a5372a233790c91164a78" :answer/id #uuid "285190e3-8c8c-5cd6-9f6c-83719d2c35da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{51}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e094f5a2-229b-5ee0-a5c7-817c4582b29f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122299/selection/befe5c309efbebd1f8cf046225b6752c361c4232623e8d3c63a7f3230bd5fe6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122299/selection/5df1e722e09c055a88f8288a681d6644451c9bb1bc22bf81932e0643a8a535ff" "q-122299/selection/937298cd9018b16cda053ff5c1f82aa544378413cbcd38ce309be5777298b48a" "q-122299/selection/befe5c309efbebd1f8cf046225b6752c361c4232623e8d3c63a7f3230bd5fe6c" "q-122299/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-122299/selection/36c923422d0040a751574fbe850eee2f3de5e3ee5e9a5372a233790c91164a78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122299" :question/id #uuid "c445f49f-fb39-57ae-9a43-7a5f707f00c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-122299" :question/problem "Ann has two shuffled $52$-card decks of playing cards, $A$ and $B.$ $2$ red cards of deck $B$ were lost. The cards of the two decks are mixed together. What is the probability that a randomly selected card from the resulting set of cards is red?\n\n*Hint: A standard $52$-card deck contains $26$ red cards and $26$ black cards.*" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be the event that the selected card is red, and let $A$ be the event that the card was one of the cards of deck $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the card was one of the cards of deck $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected card is red, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(R)=P(R\\cap A)+P(R\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(R\\cap A),$ we take the number of red cards in deck $A$ $(26)$ and divide by the total number of cards in both decks $(52+50=102).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(R\\cap A)=\\frac{26}{102}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(R\\cap {A}^{′}),$ we take the number of red cards in deck $B$ $(24)$ and divide by the total number of cards in both decks $(102).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(R\\cap {A}^{′})=\\frac{24}{102}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected card from either deck is red is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R\\cap A)+P(R\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{102}+\\frac{24}{102} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{51}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122299/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122299"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "c3d4455e-26e2-590b-a348-cf272cafd54a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "6e968ce1-8677-5ee4-adb0-490fb47c9ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "17bf85d2-d012-5408-8c1f-dadec9eb2e21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "3dab1dfc-b4c0-572e-8e5e-4a4c10efb5d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "b47b1aee-0c2e-5a7b-86ec-204b4f037bca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "67e2a31e-f187-5620-8f71-7749537bd84d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122396/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-122396/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" "q-122396/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-122396/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-122396/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-122396/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122396" :question/id #uuid "65fbcb60-cf4e-5ecd-b1d8-79e08d0131db" :question/math-academy-id "q-122396" :question/problem "A medical research center is conducting experiments to examine the relationship between cigarette smoking and cancer in a particular city. The probability that a randomly selected person is a smoker that develops cancer is $0.4,$ while the probability that it is a nonsmoker that develops cancer is $0.25.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected individual from the city develops cancer?" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that an individual develops cancer and let $A$ be the event that individual smokes. Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that an individual does not smoke.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the randomly selected individual develops the cancer, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C\\cap A)+P(C\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nWe  have \n\n$$\nP(C\\cap A)=0.4,\\,P(C\\cap {A}^{′})=0.25\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected  individual  from the city develops cancer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap A)+P(C\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =0.4+0.25 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122396/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection/b90105fbc394d22cff8af5facb45d1513f4905487a1fb39ca15b180d317aeeed" :answer/id #uuid "0bd0d403-d700-51b3-93c7-cdc7958607d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.555" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection/25096ec5768fb3e3c16b43355340403cd1a500f4fd9099de60e1b847dc1cd4b6" :answer/id #uuid "a7e69c97-762a-5077-b3e5-b09d30c41110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.725" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection/b34544a9837d181994c7a132937df1564b327d325fab23b2c613d8bcfe8cb599" :answer/id #uuid "2b54a060-5fc4-5581-8c01-9707a57fcefe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection/8a74f7804f2b58acb0a1f1c6e75a7f5c3f656af38c81f4acc315340a87349687" :answer/id #uuid "3e6ef08c-9122-59e3-9cdc-0c9d0110daca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.525" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection/1b8034731fd1f74975e77dffcdaafefd1874e8edaa65acd98af087273b86aec7" :answer/id #uuid "1a387745-e9d1-5dc2-8f6b-d9820a5548cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.325" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47ac19c1-9295-5101-880c-8e3c4e784657" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122291/selection/8a74f7804f2b58acb0a1f1c6e75a7f5c3f656af38c81f4acc315340a87349687" :answer-field/choices ["q-122291/selection/b90105fbc394d22cff8af5facb45d1513f4905487a1fb39ca15b180d317aeeed" "q-122291/selection/25096ec5768fb3e3c16b43355340403cd1a500f4fd9099de60e1b847dc1cd4b6" "q-122291/selection/b34544a9837d181994c7a132937df1564b327d325fab23b2c613d8bcfe8cb599" "q-122291/selection/8a74f7804f2b58acb0a1f1c6e75a7f5c3f656af38c81f4acc315340a87349687" "q-122291/selection/1b8034731fd1f74975e77dffcdaafefd1874e8edaa65acd98af087273b86aec7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122291" :question/id #uuid "27d3ad7e-d48b-54a5-8d61-1de17b23f16e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122291" :question/problem "A house building company has undertaken a construction job. It is known that there is a probability of $0.55$ that there will be a strike. If there won't be a strike the probability of completing the job on time is $0.8,$ if there will be a strike, the probability is $0.3.$ What is the probability that the construction job will be completed on time?" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the construction job will be completed on time, and let $S$ be the event that there will be a strike.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the construction job will be completed on time, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|S)P(S)+P(C|{S}^{′})P({S}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the probability that there will be a strike is $0.55$ and the probability that there will not be a strike is $0.45,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(S)=0.55,\\,P({S}^{′})=0.45.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that the construction job will be completed on time if there is a strike is $0.3,$ and the probability that the construction job will be completed on time if there is no strike is $0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(C|S)=0.3,\\,P(C|{S}^{′})=0.8.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability  that the construction job will be completed on time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|S)P(S)+P(C|{S}^{′})P({S}^{′}) \\\\  & =0.3\\cdot 0.55+0.8\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0.165+0.36 \\\\  & =0.525.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection/4f41bafc7ab0b7e2fc481220640460a9b38026640a803aee22f188fb150297a0" :answer/id #uuid "d51a86ea-a1ee-5927-a912-e07c14a069fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.637" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection/6b7cf3f4561487592359253492d6b17257c1c5f88f34c1539c81554b731ae1f9" :answer/id #uuid "c9a5973a-5e62-558f-8a46-ba2e836a14f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.623" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection/803f2d250891a48f4b59e2af82e5071f8ed0521d1bbdfbc2cfcce2de624d9ef1" :answer/id #uuid "2d637d35-fbcc-5364-be28-b1f129f91b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.579" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection/d3ab14771b571243272190c1d60d609a7d368a1f0740773e37d6e840df6c77ee" :answer/id #uuid "fca30c93-7a96-5054-875b-06d2bfa68242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.518" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection/d692c039a6bf6529bcde92979c7bc41fba925f8c5adecadbf51b7e7661e0d1e3" :answer/id #uuid "de2eb88a-59c6-570f-ad7d-e46e17506334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.535" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fca717d-24e4-5f62-a0b0-0d9b4fd46b9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89040/selection/803f2d250891a48f4b59e2af82e5071f8ed0521d1bbdfbc2cfcce2de624d9ef1" :answer-field/choices ["q-89040/selection/4f41bafc7ab0b7e2fc481220640460a9b38026640a803aee22f188fb150297a0" "q-89040/selection/6b7cf3f4561487592359253492d6b17257c1c5f88f34c1539c81554b731ae1f9" "q-89040/selection/803f2d250891a48f4b59e2af82e5071f8ed0521d1bbdfbc2cfcce2de624d9ef1" "q-89040/selection/d3ab14771b571243272190c1d60d609a7d368a1f0740773e37d6e840df6c77ee" "q-89040/selection/d692c039a6bf6529bcde92979c7bc41fba925f8c5adecadbf51b7e7661e0d1e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89040" :question/id #uuid "2197a11f-d70a-5147-9379-8301a61c86ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-89040" :question/problem "In a gas station, $42%$ of the clients buy regular gasoline while $58%$ buy premium gasoline. If $62%$ of the clients that buy regular gasoline paid with a credit card while $55%$ of the clients that buy premium gasoline paid with a credit card, what is the probability that a randomly selected client paid with a credit card? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen person paid with a credit card, and let $R$ be the event that the person bought regular gasoline. Then ${R}^{′}$ is the event that the person bought premium gasoline.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person paid with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $42%$ of the clients buy regular gasoline while $58%$ buy premium gasoline, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.42,\\,P({R}^{′})=0.58.\n$$\n\n- Since $62%$ of the clients that buy regular gasoline paid with a credit card while $55%$ of the clients that buy premium gasoline paid with a credit card, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|R)=0.62,\\,P(C|{R}^{′})=0.55.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected client paid with a credit card is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.62)(0.42)+(0.55)(0.58) \\\\  & ≈0.579\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89040/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection/e459c513a8ab41d90fbedd18ffc02e71387b30263f9b62ed7d74cc4e1864eeb6" :answer/id #uuid "5465c0c1-4e86-5642-8fe1-ddc0b0db7ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" :answer/id #uuid "73991856-2529-5884-90f1-e4ebe27f7215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "a2dff9bc-3cad-5e99-8e3c-1556da03de78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "ac19803a-1c42-59c8-9fac-cc047f52e61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer/id #uuid "4af3279d-1c2c-50e6-9bc7-7f1ef53fda04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "896d6b93-97e3-54ff-8aa6-dc7bde0cb061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122266/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-122266/selection/e459c513a8ab41d90fbedd18ffc02e71387b30263f9b62ed7d74cc4e1864eeb6" "q-122266/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" "q-122266/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-122266/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-122266/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122266" :question/id #uuid "9ccfae6b-552a-5354-9916-82dda86bb673" :question/math-academy-id "q-122266" :question/problem "John collects a basket of apples, only $80%$ of them are ripe. The probability that a ripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.6.$  The probability that an unripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.1.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected apple in John's collection has a worm inside?" :question/worked-solution "Let $W$ be the event that the chosen apple has a worm inside, and let $R$ be the event that the chosen apple is ripe.  \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected apple in John's collection has a worm inside, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(W)=P(W|R)P(R)+P(W|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $80%$ of the apples are ripe and $20$ are unripe, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.8,\\,P({R}^{′})=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a ripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.6,$ and the probability that an unripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(W|R)=0.6,\\,P(W|{R}^{′})=0.1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected apple in John's collection has a worm inside is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W) & =P(W|R)P(R)+P(W|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′}) \\\\  & =0.6\\cdot 0.8+0.1\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.48+0.02 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122266/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122266"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "3bd34d60-fb14-573d-a82c-7025c055dab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer/id #uuid "6d3b64b0-24de-5112-8dc7-917a4dc247bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "c3c40aa9-239a-596e-aad9-93783485ff93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "7c857ea2-3fe5-5964-9f06-cff8de46ac70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "3b924976-629f-539d-969d-b7eec1d46b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c417ae-650f-52f6-9548-5bfea8a105b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89027/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-89027/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-89027/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" "q-89027/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-89027/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-89027/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89027" :question/id #uuid "84b999b4-0afb-5f2c-8315-6aad5e7dea21" :question/math-academy-id "q-89027" :question/problem "John keeps his marbles in two boxes, box $A$ and box $B.$ Of the marbles in his collection, $\\frac{3}{4}$ of them are in box $A,$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ of them are in box $B.$ If $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the marbles in box $A$ are red and $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the marbles in box $B$ are red, what is the probability that a randomly selected marble in John's collection is red?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be the event that the chosen marble is red, and let $A$ be the event that the marble was selected from box $A.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the marble was selected from box $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected marble is red, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(R)=P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the marbles are in box $A$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ are in box $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{3}{4},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the marbles in box $A$ are red and $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the marbles in box $B$ are red, we have\n\n$$\nP(R|A)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P(R|{A}^{′})=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected marble is red is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{3}{4})+(\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+3}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection/8290eb6d62125bea63243adec1f2fbebcfb441d7359edd21727a0c82b66cbc64" :answer/id #uuid "4e9b3790-5a30-5799-aca0-cef5439e20a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection/4b19d581123670879f3f7286a8e24111d9e5eece0e30904aaaef17ef3e598617" :answer/id #uuid "f55530a0-ca6d-5c27-82ae-7e8e7b8e454a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0425" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection/71094de675b18fc530cedba96fe16240f2743c91425f8df4011ed3e47c120e38" :answer/id #uuid "ab1dfe68-966a-566d-85ef-a113794b46f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0325" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "18c12ccd-0796-5f80-a987-4dd885edf5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection/15c80f56bb9624698cb5ae66a8f9d6825dab1526a47faa00abc6b8b10bd477da" :answer/id #uuid "3a05e34a-131b-50b5-9ec4-4d702741ba54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1fc0c6f-c75f-5802-b5b7-f0aec7c451f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122293/selection/4b19d581123670879f3f7286a8e24111d9e5eece0e30904aaaef17ef3e598617" :answer-field/choices ["q-122293/selection/8290eb6d62125bea63243adec1f2fbebcfb441d7359edd21727a0c82b66cbc64" "q-122293/selection/4b19d581123670879f3f7286a8e24111d9e5eece0e30904aaaef17ef3e598617" "q-122293/selection/71094de675b18fc530cedba96fe16240f2743c91425f8df4011ed3e47c120e38" "q-122293/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-122293/selection/15c80f56bb9624698cb5ae66a8f9d6825dab1526a47faa00abc6b8b10bd477da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122293" :question/id #uuid "abb80d0d-3cb2-5dfa-b275-cc5f2ea2f90e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122293" :question/problem "Two machines ${M}_{1}$ and ${M}_{2}$ in a certain factory produce $75%$ and $25%,$ respectively, of the total daily output of electronic tubes. It is known that $4%$ of the tubes produced by machine ${M}_{1}$ and that $5%$ of those produced by ${M}_{2}$ are defective. What is the probability that a randomly picked tube from a day's production is defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that the picked electronic tube is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the electronic tube is produced by machine ${M}_{1}.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the electronic tube is produced by machine ${M}_{2}.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly picked tube from a day's production is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine ${M}_{1}$ produces $75%$ of the total daily output of electronic tubes and ${M}_{2}$ the remaining $25%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.75,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.25.\n$$\n\n- Since $4%$ of the tubes produced by machine ${M}_{1}$ are defective, and $5%$ of the tubes produced by machine ${M}_{2}$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.04,\\,P(D|{A}^{′})=0.05.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly picked tube from a day's production is defective is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.04)(0.75)+(0.05)(0.25) \\\\  & =0.0425.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122293/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "3d0ee564-987f-5268-a8a1-574e405b637c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "5beed6cb-ec10-5672-b127-bf45985e5d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "ae6907da-1dc3-5cbd-84a7-9fa76a8537c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "1227a403-c8c1-55ed-abb4-871261ed4b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "d17c6fb6-e976-558b-8e98-3c2e201053b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75cb7c81-8945-5557-a12c-35154d92b98c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89051/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-89051/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-89051/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-89051/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-89051/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-89051/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89051" :question/id #uuid "c87ef258-ca2e-5999-aa06-94a6a0d92ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-89051" :question/problem "Daniel has a desk with two drawers, drawer $A$ and drawer $B.$ Of the total amount of pens that he has, $\\frac{4}{5}$ of them are in drawer $A,$ and $\\frac{1}{5}$ are in drawer $B.$ Also, $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the pens in drawer $A$ are blue, and Daniel knows that $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the pens in both drawers are blue. What is the probability that a randomly selected pen from drawer $B$ is blue?" :question/worked-solution "Let $U$ be the event that the chosen pen is blue, and let $A$ be the event that the pen was selected from drawer $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the pen was selected from drawer $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected pen is blue, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(U)=P(U|A)P(A)+P(U|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{4}{5}$ of the pens are in drawer $A$ and $\\frac{1}{5}$ are in drawer $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{4}{5},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the pens in drawer $A$ are blue, we have\n\n$$\nP(U|A)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the pens on the desk drawers are blue, we have\n\n$$\nP(U)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(U|{D}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U) & =P(U|A)P(A)+P(U|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =(\\frac{3}{4})(\\frac{4}{5})+P(U|{A}^{′})(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}P(U|{A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}P(U|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{10-9}{15} \\\\ P(U|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected pen from drawer $B$ is blue is $\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89051/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-89054"] :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that the chosen student obtained the top grade, and let $A$ be the event that the student is from Group $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the student is from Group $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student obtained the top grade, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $35%$ of her students are in Group $A$ and $65%$ are in Group $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.35,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.65.\n$$\n\n- Since $20%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.20.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top  grade is $0.265,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=0.265.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.265 & =(0.20)(0.35)+P(G|{A}^{′})(0.65) \\\\ 0.265 & =0.07+0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.65P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.195 \\\\ P(G|{A}^{′}) & =0.30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected student from Group $B$ obtained the top grade is $0.30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer/id #uuid "a4f2bb2f-83a1-54e3-adc7-e85a3bbb21f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection/c1947e67097a32b8f5310015f8a63ebdf6aa2d5dc852c008352aef2569b877cf" :answer/id #uuid "b045c791-f026-5373-b76c-207765192819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection/c3c73e94796ef446faf960d5ccd1311009de19f171f5e5a8d459da0b2bbef96f" :answer/id #uuid "8ce4098a-0f83-57b2-b691-59b426186341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection/6c3fe5936b48b6895a0cca907277410fe16fa6a16cf280ebb305d391a97cd1f3" :answer/id #uuid "21b21ac7-732b-5984-96da-063bf5e5a17d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection/8cdaa067f375a830d5b1e57b5029529ea90227c752cbf890839edae4bfd1a326" :answer/id #uuid "2b1d149a-cd2f-5121-ba46-797875516a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "68f95639-8c1d-58bb-ba31-3c7e564022c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89044/selection/6c3fe5936b48b6895a0cca907277410fe16fa6a16cf280ebb305d391a97cd1f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-89044/selection/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" "q-89044/selection/c1947e67097a32b8f5310015f8a63ebdf6aa2d5dc852c008352aef2569b877cf" "q-89044/selection/c3c73e94796ef446faf960d5ccd1311009de19f171f5e5a8d459da0b2bbef96f" "q-89044/selection/6c3fe5936b48b6895a0cca907277410fe16fa6a16cf280ebb305d391a97cd1f3" "q-89044/selection/8cdaa067f375a830d5b1e57b5029529ea90227c752cbf890839edae4bfd1a326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89044" :question/id #uuid "52bfa097-4cee-51bc-97ec-d6074dab330f" :question/math-academy-id "q-89044" :question/problem "Jacob has two email accounts, account $A$ and account $B.$ In account $A$ he receives $40%$ of his emails and he receives the remaining $60%$ in account $B.$ Approximately $30%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam and $36%$ of the emails received in both accounts are spam. What is the probability that a randomly selected email from account $B$ is spam? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen email is spam, and let $A$ be the event that the email selected is from account $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the email selected is from account $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $40%$ of the emails are received in account $A$ and the remaining $60%$ in account $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.40,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.60.\n$$\n\n- Since $30%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam, we have \n\n$$\nP(S|A)=0.30.\n$$\n\n- Since $36%$ of the emails received in both accounts are spam, we have \n\n$$\nP(S)=0.36.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(S|{A}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.36 & =(0.30)(0.40)+P(S|{A}^{′})(0.60) \\\\ 0.36 & =0.12+0.6P(S|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.6P(S|{A}^{′}) & =0.24 \\\\ P(S|{A}^{′}) & =0.40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected email from account $B$ is spam is $0.40.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89044/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89044"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "fbb9eda2-99c2-5be7-a950-84e056caeca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection/e4267992b1782365f5817e630b24491092dc1c1da024bac79325760c40e35e4f" :answer/id #uuid "f45adc33-d1b6-5b7b-ad2c-1b9bc9d454ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "de716bd1-4cfc-58ba-85ba-302ec32ffc75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "d7a97ae1-bce4-5bda-bbe9-c2d28cfb77ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "d43e7829-6106-5687-b061-b764a19edd27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d5d8d4-e0fd-5890-943c-90195526c61a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89045/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer-field/choices ["q-89045/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-89045/selection/e4267992b1782365f5817e630b24491092dc1c1da024bac79325760c40e35e4f" "q-89045/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-89045/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" "q-89045/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89045" :question/id #uuid "f25294cd-a31f-5ed2-b885-814c97b7c2c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-89045" :question/problem "James keeps his marbles in two boxes, box $A$ and box $B.$ In total, $\\frac{3}{4}$ of his marbles are in box $A,$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ are in box $B.$ If $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the marbles in box $A$ are red, and $\\frac{7}{10}$ of the marbles in both boxes are red, what is the probability that a randomly selected marble from box $B$ is red?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be the event that the chosen marble is red, and let $A$ be the event that the marble was selected from box $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the marble was selected from box $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected marble is red, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(R)=P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the marbles are in box $A$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ are in box $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=\\frac{3}{4},\\,P({A}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the marbles in box $A$ are red, we have\n\n$$\nP(R|A)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{7}{10}$ of the marbles in both boxes are red, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(R|{A}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =(\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{3}{4})+P(R|{A}^{′})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}P(R|{A}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}P(R|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ P(R|{A}^{′}) & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected marble from box $B$ is red is $\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89045/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89045"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection/dbbd2ab186e6446437720ddefa77970e71256eaf21337e33e8b16e90376bea90" :answer/id #uuid "42c8a18f-124b-513b-b630-06a5e0912eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection/22bbee0d8e9610e940e635938755e10bd27ffea1adddb9664ad643e6998d9bdf" :answer/id #uuid "d28c05ad-8b8e-59a9-a245-a897da2ea651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" :answer/id #uuid "7fd9e616-412a-52e2-ae68-fd193240878b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "6a1eb6dd-d98a-56a5-a528-407717fb370a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779" :answer/id #uuid "ab403a0f-1c5e-5379-825b-efd3faa747c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b31402d-c144-5067-a816-f376c5650651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122405/selection/22bbee0d8e9610e940e635938755e10bd27ffea1adddb9664ad643e6998d9bdf" :answer-field/choices ["q-122405/selection/dbbd2ab186e6446437720ddefa77970e71256eaf21337e33e8b16e90376bea90" "q-122405/selection/22bbee0d8e9610e940e635938755e10bd27ffea1adddb9664ad643e6998d9bdf" "q-122405/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" "q-122405/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" "q-122405/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122405" :question/id #uuid "4a132b6f-cc89-532a-89e1-2c7f30052adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122405" :question/problem "John collects a basket of apples, but only $80%$ of them are ripe. The probability that a ripe apple has a worm inside it is $0.6.$  The probability that a randomly selected apple has a worm inside it is $0.5.$ What is the probability of a randomly selected unripe apple having a worm inside it?" :question/worked-solution "Let $W$ be the event that the chosen apple has a worm inside, and let $R$ be the event that the chosen apple is ripe.  \n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected apple in John's collection has a worm inside, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(W)=P(W|R)P(R)+P(W|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $80%$ of the apples are ripe and $20%$ are unripe, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.8,\\,P({R}^{′})=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a ripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.6$,  we have\n\n$$\nP(W|R)=0.6.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected apple in John's collection has a worm inside is $0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(W)=0.5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(W|{R}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W) & =P(W|R)P(R)+P(W|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.5 & =(0.6)(0.8)+P(W|{R}^{′})(0.2) \\\\ 0.5 & =0.48+0.2P(W|{R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.02 & =0.2P(W|{R}^{′}) \\\\ P(W|{R}^{′}) & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected unripe apple has a worm inside the apple is $0.1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122405/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
